            "insights": "<ul>\n  <li>Maharashtra leads in order volume with 465 orders, followed by Karnataka with 166 and Telangana with 142.</li>\n  <li>Maharashtra’s order count is 323 higher than Telangana’s, a 69.5% difference, and 299 higher than Karnataka’s, a 64.3% difference.</li>\n  <li>In revenue, Maharashtra generated $259,580, which is 62.3% greater than Telangana’s $97,838 and 54.1% greater than Karnataka’s $119,235.</li>\n  <li>Karnataka’s average order value of $718 is 28.7% above Maharashtra’s $558 and 4.2% above Telangana’s $689.</li>\n  <li>Compared to the Maharashtra baseline, Telangana’s average order value is 23.4% higher, while Karnataka’s is 28.7% higher.</li>\n  <li>Payment mode patterns show COD dominance in Maharashtra (290 COD vs 175 PrePaid) and Telangana (99 COD vs 43 PrePaid), whereas Karnataka splits nearly evenly with 89 COD and 77 PrePaid.</li>\n  <li>Order status indicates strong fulfillment: Maharashtra shipped 393 orders (84% of its total), Telangana shipped 128 (90%), and Karnataka shipped 146 (88%).</li>\n  <li>Top city concentrations differ: Maharashtra’s demand is spread across Mumbai (112), MUMBAI (92), and many other towns; Telangana is heavily Hyderabad‑centric (90 orders); Karnataka focuses on Bangalore (84 orders).</li>\n  <li>Overall winners by metric are Maharashtra for volume and revenue, while Karnataka tops average order value.</li>\n  <li>Relative to the Maharashtra baseline, Telangana’s order count is 69.5% lower, revenue 62.3% lower, and average order value 23.4% higher; Karnataka’s order count is 64.3% lower, revenue 54.1% lower, and average order value 28.7% higher.</li>\n  <li>Actionable insight: Boost order volume in Telangana and Karnataka to narrow the gap, and leverage Karnataka’s higher average order value to drive additional revenue growth.</li>\n  <li>Consider expanding PrePaid options in Maharashtra and Telangana to diversify payment modes and potentially increase average order value.</li>\n</ul>",
